357:## 8. Receipt v2, cache identity, and mixed schema-7 builds\n1359:### 8.1 Unsubstituted external receipt input\n1433:### 8.2 Substituted external receipt input\n1490:### 8.3 Mixed command behavior\n1503:## 9. Marker v3, status, repair, deduplication, and GC\n1566:### 9.1 Snapshot and artifact keys\n1574:### 9.2 Read-only status\n1594:### 9.3 Repair\n1605:### 9.4 Garbage collection roots\n1616:## 10. Deterministic build, install, PATH, and rollback\n1645:## 11. Signing and notarization boundary\n1665:## 12. Future closed-driver rule\n1686:## 13. Threat model\n1688:### 13.1 Adversary-controlled\n1696:### 13.2 Trusted computing base\n1705:### 13.3 Required controls\n1730:## 14. Exact impact on existing board work\n1734:### 14.1 Existing curator-spec schema-6 story\n1751:### 14.2 Existing Curator implementation story\n1765:### 14.3 Existing cocoaskills implementation story\n1771:### 14.4 Existing interoperability story\n1785:## 15. Rejected alternatives\n1810:## 16. Primary-source register\n1861:## 17. Validation and independent-review checks\n1921:### 17.1 Producer verification evidence\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
