d shim is manager-owned and resolves exactly to the protected artifact\n1128:selected by marker v3. It MUST NOT point into a Git object database, frozen\n1129:snapshot, checkout, staging directory, or script runtime. The artifact is one\n1130:regular singly linked executable whose path, hash, and size match its receipt.\n1132:Validation uses no shell, executable search, or artifact execution. Repository\n1138:Read-only status derives the current manifest and operator substitution plan,\n1139:validates marker v3, revalidates protected snapshot/artifact boundaries,\n1140:recomputes every available source digest, receipt input/key, receipt hash, and\n1141:artifact relationship, and structurally validates shims and PATH exposure. It\n1146:Identity, commit, digest, target, substitution, receipt, artifact, shim, or\n1147:boundary mismatch is non-current. Missing required protected evidence is not\n1148:current. An implementation MAY distinguish `unknown` from drift when evidence\n1149:cannot be read, but it MUST NOT report current and checking status returns\n1152:Repair repeats the current effective acquisition, object proof, freeze, audit,\n1155:bytes by changing permissions, recomputing a marker, or trusting a consistent\n1156:receipt.\n1159:boundary. Valid marker v3 records mark referenced local skill snapshots,\n1160:complete external snapshot keys, receipt/artifact keys, and manager-generated\n1161:shim relationships. In-flight journals mark every snapshot/artifact needed for\n1163:is not a root. Unreadable markers/journals or unprovable references retain\n1165:artifact bytes.\n1169:The following semantic codes are stable and MUST remain distinguishable in\n1182:| `build_repository_local_linked_worktree_unsupported` | Local administration uses linked-worktree state |\n1184:| `build_repository_local_format_unsupported` | Local config, ref storage, extension, promisor, or partial-clone state is unsupported |\n1187:Schema/version/driver, descriptor, identity/ref gramma